## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card on Hover</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Container that gives the card a 3‑D perspective */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 800px;          /* How far the viewer is from the card */
  margin: 50px auto;           /* Center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – front & back sides */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d; /* Keep children in 3‑D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Front side */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hide the back when facing away */
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* 4️⃣  Front side styling */
.card .front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* 5️⃣  Back side styling – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card .back {
  background: #4a90e2;
  color: #fff;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
}

/* 6️⃣  Hover effect – rotate the whole card 180° */
.card-wrapper:hover .card {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on the wrapper | Gives depth so the rotation looks 3‑D. |
| 2 | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on the card | Keeps child elements (front/back) in 3‑D space. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the side that is turned away from the viewer. |
| 4 | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on the back | Positions the back side opposite the front. |
| 5 | `transition` on the card | Smoothly animates the rotation. |
| 6 | Hover selector | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside `.front` and `.back`.  
If you want a flip around the X‑axis instead, change `rotateY` to `rotateX` everywhere.
